= Preprints and Publications

My research is primarily concerned with finite groups. Much of my work deals with the values taken by 
group characters, so my research has a somewhat number-theoretic flavor. I am also interested in the theory
of permutation groups and related combinatorial subjects.

- [https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.12326 On a question of Navarro on the field of values of characters of solvable groups], arXiv preprint (2026).
- [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.26463 A determination of /B/-groups of order p^4], arXiv preprint (2026).
- [https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.10888 Character Values and Conductors of Low-rank Groups of Lie Type], with N. N. Hung, arXiv preprint (2026).
- [https://doi.org/10.1515/jgth-2025-0161 Generalized Characters and Prime Graphs], to appear in the /Journal of Group Theory/, (2026).
- [https://doi.org/10.1007/s00013-025-02212-z Answer to a question of Hung and Tiep on conductors of cyclotomic integers], /Arch. Math. (Basel)/ *126*(3) (2026).
- [https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.23637 A block-theoretic proof of Burnside's Normal $p$-complement Theorem], arXiv preprint (2025).
- [https://huskiecommons.lib.niu.edu/allgraduate-thesesdissertations/8208/ On values taken by characters of finite groups], dissertation (2026).

= Employment History

I am currently employed as an assistant professor of mathematics at Little Priest Tribal College in
Winnebago, Nebraska. Prior to working here, I worked as a graduate teaching assistant at Northern 
Illinois University and as an adjunct instructor at Kishwaukee College. For a more detailed look at
my teaching experience, click [teaching.html here].

= Education
- Ph.D. in Mathematics, Northern Illinois University, 2026
- M.S. in Mathematics, Northern Illinois University, 2024
- B.Sc in Mathematics, Northern Illinois University, 2021

